# Tests must pass before opening a pull request

Before opening a pull request (or marking a draft PR ready for review), confirm that tests for the change pass.

1. Identify the tests that cover the code you changed (and any closely related packages or components).
2. Run those tests locally and wait for a clean exit. Do not open or update the PR as "ready" while tests are failing or still running.
3. Prefer targeted commands for the changed area, for example:
   - Frontend: `yarn jest --no-watch path/to/file` (or the feature/package under test)
   - Backend: `go test -run TestName ./pkg/services/myservice/` (or the package under test)
4. If you added or updated automated tests as part of the change, those new/updated tests must pass.
5. If tests fail, fix the failures (or the tests, when they are wrong) and re-run until they pass. Do not open a PR that you know has failing tests.
6. In the pull request description, briefly note which tests you ran and that they passed. If you could not run a relevant suite (missing deps, environment limits, or similar), say what you skipped and why — do not silently omit verification.

This rule applies to cloud agents and any agent workflow that creates or updates pull requests.
